    "done_when": "Census every measured accuracy result of the nova forward map, topology read and forward solve against plasma cell count, to judge whether raising the cell count (from about 2,000 cells upward on the H200) would meet the acceptance clauses without the high-order machinery the current plans build. Done when the report holds: (1) a table with one row per measured quantity and resolution (at least the certificate rungs 132, 300, 550, 1074 and 2616 cells, and any other cell counts measured anywhere in nova), giving the quantity (map fidelity at the analytic state, per-cell membership error split into smooth and saddle-neighbourhood cells, axis and X-point position error in pitches and metres, limiter contact error, global and constraint-row residual, boundary distance, plasma current error), the case (weak-rotation limited, diverted single-null, centroid-constrained rows, MAST and DIII-D frames, CORSICA 130506), the representation used (chord, exact clip, quadratic, saddle normal form) and the source; (2) for each quantity with three or more resolutions, the fitted convergence order and the cell count at which refinement alone would reach the plan acceptance bound for it (the converged-forward-solve section 6 table: map fidelity 1e-2, axis and X-point within one pitch, residual 1e-12, and the derived row tolerances), stating where an order below one makes refinement impractical (for example the half-order saddle measurement); (3) a verdict per acceptance clause: met by refinement to at most about 10,000 cells, met only with a higher-order representation, or not determinable from existing evidence, with the measurement that would decide it. Work read-only: read plans under docs/plans, research under docs/research, evidence fragments under docs/evidence, receipts and figures under docs/figures and the GPFS evidence root, run directories under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs that belong to project nova, the committed ledger docs/state/nova, and the source under nova/ and tests/. Every number you report carries its source (file path and anchor, or run id and log), and every claim that is an inference rather than a measurement says so. Deliver the report as one markdown file at the assigned write path, with the required tables, and write the manifest with status complete, blocked or failed, which you set yourself.",
